        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep exact tool allowlists on owning factories",
        "body": "Closes #104208\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users or jobs with exact embedded-run tool allowlists could lose the requested tool when its hand-maintained factory classification had drifted. `transcripts` was routed away from its core factory, while plugin-owned `canvas` was routed away from plugin construction.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCore tool identity and factory family now live in one lightweight typed catalog. The attempt planner classifies each normalized allowlist once, while plugin, MCP, and LSP discovery remain on their existing runtime paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExact allowlists now expose `transcripts` and `canvas` through their actual owners. Future core-tool additions have catalog-to-factory regression coverage instead of requiring parallel name maps to remain synchronized manually.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Source-built ephemeral Gateway E2E at exact head `fe131d2951de20ff0e8488f4b8bc552e42996b16` under Node 24: two ordinary CLI-created one-shot isolated cron jobs completed with status `ok`; captured model requests advertised exactly `transcripts` for `toolsAllow: [\"transcripts\"]` and exactly `canvas` for `toolsAllow: [\"canvas\"]`. Only the model transport was mocked; Gateway, scheduler, embedded runner, planner, and core/plugin factories were real.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx7tfhjkkf9czp9y7b48mcjf`: 84/84 focused planner and core-factory tests passed.\n- Same Testbox: 72/72 broader agent-tool construction tests passed.\n- Same Testbox: `pnpm check:changed` passed, including production/test typechecks, changed-file lint, import-cycle and architecture guards.\n- `autoreview --mode local --engine codex --thinking high`: clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Distill/Greybeard pass replaced repeated family scans and linear descriptor lookup with one normalized classification pass plus a process-stable map.\n- Rebased onto current `main` without conflict; stable patch id remained `194567780968c1c7b85bba4f1dee3fb8ed7d2cb5`.\n- Exact-head PR CI run `29142082269`: 44 jobs passed. The sole failure is unrelated `src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts` inventory drift; this PR touches only `src/agents/**`.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Implementation and every accepted review decision were manually inspected.\n",
